{
    "background_story": "Kayla was a free-spirited artist who lived life on her own terms. She spent her days babbling to anyone who would listen about her latest creative endeavors, from painting to pottery. Her friends and family would often joke that she could talk the ears off a cornfield, but they loved her for it. Kayla's babbling was infectious, and she had a way of making everyone around her feel seen and heard. One day, while chatting with a stranger at a coffee shop, Kayla stumbled upon an idea for a community art project. She spent the next hour babbling excitedly to the stranger, who turned out to be a local art curator. The project took off, and soon Kayla's art was showcased in galleries across the city. Her non-stop chatter had led to a chance encounter that changed her life forever.",
